# Paths an indexer skips, and that an agent does not read. Same syntax as
# .gitignore. Git's own list is .gitignore; this one also names tracked files
# that are generated and not worth reading, and personal notes (`*.local.md`).

# YAGIT_ROOT — the boundary the daemon refuses to open outside of. Machine
# local and never committed; .env.example documents every key it holds.
.env

# The session token, and the end-to-end stack log: it traces every git
# command the daemon ran and every repository path it touched. `./do test
# e2e` prints that log itself when the stack fails to start, which is the
# one moment it is worth reading.
.yagit/

# Dependencies, binaries, and the frontend build. `./do build` reproduces
# all three.
web/node_modules/
dist/
internal/assets/dist/

# Generated, and reviewed by tooling rather than by eye.
web/package-lock.json

# Personal notes for this checkout.
*.local.md
